# ── Environment variables & credentials ──
# PATTERN-based on purpose. This block used to enumerate individual filenames
# (.env.local.backup, .env.backup, …), so any variant nobody had thought of yet
# was silently trackable: `.env.vercel.production` — a Vercel export holding
# PRODUCTION Firebase service-account credentials — sat untracked-and-unignored
# in the working tree, one `git add -A` from being committed. Cover the shape,
# not the filename; opt tracked templates back in by negation below.
.env
.env.*
*.env
*.env.*

# Intentionally tracked templates. These must contain placeholders only —
# never a real value. Anything else matching .env* stays ignored above.
!.env.example
!*.env.example

# Refresh script output
scripts/output/
scripts/test-results/*
!scripts/test-results/20260427-224157Z/
!scripts/test-results/20260427-224157Z/**

